{"id": "food-science-b-curated-frq-001", "valid": true, "deterministic_errors": [], "judge": {"solvable": true, "independent_answer": "Fresh pineapple contains active protease enzymes (like bromelain) that break down the gelatin’s protein chains so they can’t form a solid gel. In canned pineapple, heat from processing denatures and inactivates these enzymes, so the gelatin proteins stay intact and can cross-link to form a firm gel.", "science_correct": true, "division_b_appropriate": true, "food_science_relevant": true, "difficulty_match": true, "reasoning_depth_match": true, "source_level_calibrated": true, "source_scope_faithful": true, "single_unambiguous_answer": true, "competition_faithful": true, "style_faithful": true, "concise": true, "distractors_plausible": true, "safety_appropriate": true, "plan_faithful": true, "novel": true, "issues": [], "answer_agrees": true, "answer_equivalence": {"compatible": true, "issues": []}}}
{"id": "food-science-b-curated-frq-002", "valid": true, "deterministic_errors": [], "judge": {"solvable": true, "independent_answer": "Lactose intolerance is caused by lack of the enzyme lactase, so undigested lactose in regular milk causes gas, bloating, and diarrhea. In lactose-free milk the lactose is already broken down, so there is no problem. A milk-protein allergy is an immune reaction to the milk proteins (like casein or whey), which are still present in lactose-free milk, so the allergic person will still react even if the lactose is removed.", "science_correct": true, "division_b_appropriate": true, "food_science_relevant": true, "difficulty_match": true, "reasoning_depth_match": true, "source_level_calibrated": true, "source_scope_faithful": true, "single_unambiguous_answer": true, "competition_faithful": true, "style_faithful": true, "concise": true, "distractors_plausible": true, "safety_appropriate": true, "plan_faithful": true, "novel": true, "issues": [], "answer_agrees": true, "answer_equivalence": {"compatible": true, "issues": []}}}
{"id": "food-science-b-curated-frq-003", "valid": true, "deterministic_errors": [], "judge": {"solvable": true, "independent_answer": "Stirring while the fudge cools causes sucrose to crystallize; agitation gives many nucleation sites so lots of small sugar crystals form, making the texture grainy instead of staying as a smooth, mostly uncrystallized sugar phase.", "science_correct": true, "division_b_appropriate": true, "food_science_relevant": true, "difficulty_match": true, "reasoning_depth_match": true, "source_level_calibrated": true, "source_scope_faithful": true, "single_unambiguous_answer": true, "competition_faithful": true, "style_faithful": true, "concise": true, "distractors_plausible": true, "safety_appropriate": true, "plan_faithful": true, "novel": true, "issues": [], "answer_agrees": true, "answer_equivalence": {"compatible": true, "issues": []}}}
{"id": "food-science-b-curated-frq-004", "valid": true, "deterministic_errors": [], "judge": {"solvable": true, "independent_answer": "Vitamin A; it is fat‑soluble, so it is stored in body fat and the liver, while excess water‑soluble vitamin C is not stored and is mostly excreted in urine.", "science_correct": true, "division_b_appropriate": true, "food_science_relevant": true, "difficulty_match": true, "reasoning_depth_match": true, "source_level_calibrated": true, "source_scope_faithful": true, "single_unambiguous_answer": true, "competition_faithful": true, "style_faithful": true, "concise": true, "distractors_plausible": true, "safety_appropriate": true, "plan_faithful": true, "novel": true, "issues": [], "answer_agrees": true}}
{"id": "food-science-b-curated-frq-005", "valid": true, "deterministic_errors": [], "judge": {"solvable": true, "independent_answer": "Independent variable: sucrose concentration of the jam.\nDependent variable: time it takes the jam to drain through the funnel (or flow rate).\nTwo controlled conditions (examples): use the same funnel and container setup for all trials, and keep the jam samples at the same temperature. (Other acceptable controls: same total jam volume, same type/recipe of jam base, same starting height in the funnel.)", "science_correct": true, "division_b_appropriate": true, "food_science_relevant": true, "difficulty_match": true, "reasoning_depth_match": true, "source_level_calibrated": true, "source_scope_faithful": true, "single_unambiguous_answer": true, "competition_faithful": true, "style_faithful": true, "concise": true, "distractors_plausible": true, "safety_appropriate": true, "plan_faithful": true, "novel": true, "issues": [], "answer_agrees": true, "answer_equivalence": {"compatible": true, "issues": []}}}
